Here, the reader is working as an array and we get the value of the database table columns
sequentially from the index. As we can see from the following table structure in the
database, it has four columns, Id, FirstName, LastName, and Age:
These columns will be mapped one after another. reader[0] refers to the Id column,
reader[1] refers to the Firstname column, and so on.
The statement we have written will print the value of the FirstName column, where it will
find reader[1]. It will then print the value of the LastName column, where it will find
reader[2].
If this array index is confusing for you and if you want more readability, feel free to use
named indexes instead of numbers:
